  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the maintainer, I want the SwiftHFR store material ready (description, keywords, « Nouveautés », TestFlight « What to Test », screenshots, support URL, privacy answers), written for HFR's audience and consistent with the app, so that the first TestFlight and App Store releases go out with a proper listing. (Operator, 2026-11-18: comes last, kept aside; claimed by the operator to hold it.)\n\n### Scope\n\n- French texts for HFR forum members: the description, keywords, the « Nouveautés » template per version, and the TestFlight « What to Test » notes. They follow the legacy release-notes habit (`push_realease.md` on legacy `master`, LOT-161).\n- iPhone and iPad screenshots taken from a clean `user2` session. No real pseudos or private content: anonymised content only (FIXTURES rules).\n- Support URL, privacy (App Privacy answers consistent with what the app sends: HFR, rehost and Giphy hosts, iCloud KVS), age rating (user-generated content, LOT-159).\n- The App Store information goes in the existing HFR+ record if that is ezzz's choice (see #1134).\n\n### Depends on\n\n- #1134 (the operator's access in App Store Connect)\n- LOT-159 (#249, App Review and UGC compliance) for the age rating and moderation wording\n- LOT-161 (#251) for the version numbering\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
